  "script": "Meet the Dodge Viper SRT-10, a beast with a staggering 500 horsepower. Under the hood is an 8.3-liter V10 engine that screams performance. With 525 lb-ft of torque, it's all about raw, unfiltered power. Originally starting around $85,000, you can find them today for about $50,000. The Viper faces off against the Chevrolet Corvette Z06, boasting 505 horsepower to the Viper's 500. At N\u00fcrburgring in 2008, the Viper set a record for fastest lap by a production car at the time. Ralph Gilles spearheaded the design, ensuring it stayed true to its aggressive roots. So, do you crave the raw power of the Viper, or the agility of its rivals?",
